WEBVTT

00:04.750 --> 00:10.070
Ignorant and purposeless, worth less than the dust beneath our feet...

00:10.070 --> 00:14.180
That is who you sinners of Falaina truly are.

00:36.240 --> 00:37.890
Masoo, are you okay?

00:38.410 --> 00:39.510
I'm just fine.

00:44.270 --> 00:48.600
<i>Damn, I didn't expect it to progress this quickly.</i>

00:50.850 --> 00:53.570
<i>Guys, we're counting on you.</i>

00:54.300 --> 00:57.070
<i>The rest of us are hitting our limit.</i>

01:16.160 --> 01:18.590
Hey, old man! They'll see you!

01:19.440 --> 01:21.350
Masoo, that's dangerous!

01:21.350 --> 01:22.060
Kuchiba!

01:36.770 --> 01:40.070
She was always devoted to others.

01:44.880 --> 01:48.500
All she wished was for the people of our island to live happily.

01:48.990 --> 01:54.250
She even sacrificed herself for that happiness...

02:03.010 --> 02:05.770
Can you understand the weight of that life?

02:06.330 --> 02:08.240
She wasn't...

02:08.940 --> 02:12.690
She wasn't someone the likes of you had any right to kill!

02:22.660 --> 02:25.750
What the hell are you doing, you dumbass beanpole?!

02:25.750 --> 02:27.830
D-Dumbass beanpole?

02:30.040 --> 02:31.420
Don't get in my way!

02:31.420 --> 02:33.630
You wanna throw your life away, old man?!

02:33.630 --> 02:34.380
Shut up!

02:34.380 --> 02:35.790
<i>You</i> shut up!

02:35.790 --> 02:37.760
You can't even use thymia!

02:37.760 --> 02:39.090
What?!

02:39.090 --> 02:40.090
Unseemly.

02:41.620 --> 02:42.720
How unseemly.

02:45.090 --> 02:50.060
Humans with emotions are always full of resentment and rage.

02:50.480 --> 02:52.320
How very unseemly.

02:52.940 --> 02:55.980
What's wrong with being unseemly? What's more...

02:56.900 --> 03:01.280
Someone who kills people with their face hidden has no right to say that!

03:03.280 --> 03:04.700
It's a child.

03:06.540 --> 03:07.950
What's wrong?

03:08.360 --> 03:09.660
Can't you kill me?

03:24.800 --> 03:28.300
I'll take revenge... for Lady Taisha.

03:31.770 --> 03:34.400
Just... stop.

03:34.940 --> 03:36.150
Please!

03:43.380 --> 03:48.370
I wonder what my daughter would be like by now if she were alive.

03:57.960 --> 03:59.220
Pagoni.

04:14.790 --> 04:15.480
Ouni!

04:20.590 --> 04:25.070
<i>The daimons of Falaina... I suppose they were just a superstition.</i>

04:25.070 --> 04:26.200
<i>Worthless.</i>

04:26.680 --> 04:27.730
Give me that.

04:32.480 --> 04:35.710
You, more worthless than the dust above the sands,

04:35.710 --> 04:37.080
just disappear!

04:37.080 --> 04:39.500
Even I understand that much!

04:39.890 --> 04:42.420
We're trapped on a tiny island

04:42.420 --> 04:44.430
and don't know anything about the world!

04:45.380 --> 04:47.220
We can't change anything!

04:47.220 --> 04:49.500
That's who we are!

04:50.470 --> 04:53.270
But I'll escape that mud boat!

04:53.270 --> 04:57.230
So don't get in my way, you baldie!

05:07.210 --> 05:08.030
Ouni!

05:37.590 --> 05:39.770
You guys can't stop us!

05:44.570 --> 05:47.820
We're the bowel moles!

05:54.910 --> 05:56.960
Bring it on!

05:56.960 --> 06:01.090
When Ouni and me are together, we're the strongest!

06:01.090 --> 06:04.100
Don't you ever look down on us again!

06:07.360 --> 06:08.200
Ouni?!

06:08.650 --> 06:10.260
Are you okay, Ou—

06:20.780 --> 06:25.240
Why are you hesitating before these rats?
Finish them off already.

06:27.560 --> 06:30.820
We were... alwa—

06:33.100 --> 06:34.790
...together.

06:37.560 --> 06:38.330
Ou...

06:51.100 --> 06:52.050
Nibi?

06:59.500 --> 07:02.130
<i>I'll take you to the outside world!</i>

07:12.030 --> 07:13.160
Thymia?!

07:19.500 --> 07:22.330
How? It's impossible!

07:22.710 --> 07:25.710
An aura... in the nous passage?

07:29.670 --> 07:31.430
Ouni! Nibi!

07:31.430 --> 07:32.550
Chakuro, look out!

07:42.800 --> 07:43.940
A daimon...

08:13.510 --> 08:14.390
Lykos!

08:14.720 --> 08:15.430
Chakuro!

08:27.060 --> 08:31.190
Th-This mustn't be allowed to happen...

08:31.190 --> 08:34.950
That's it... it's because we broke the taboo!

08:34.950 --> 08:37.900
It's all Orka's fault!

08:37.900 --> 08:42.040
He caused the daimon to awaken!

08:56.440 --> 08:59.330
Hey, Mojamoja! What's with all this?

08:59.330 --> 09:00.600
How should I know?!

09:01.040 --> 09:02.600
Chakki...

09:11.630 --> 09:12.280
Lykos!

09:15.130 --> 09:17.080
Lykos, are you okay?

09:21.810 --> 09:24.830
Ouni! Ouni, where are you?

10:08.290 --> 10:09.500
Nibi!

10:26.780 --> 10:29.540
I was scared you'd leave me behind,

10:30.200 --> 10:33.230
but I guess it ended up being the other way around.

10:34.150 --> 10:35.060
Nibi!

10:41.110 --> 10:43.550
Sorry, but you can't.

10:43.550 --> 10:45.650
I can't let you on this boat.

10:46.540 --> 10:48.320
Buki... Aijiro...

10:53.310 --> 10:54.420
You know...

10:56.620 --> 10:58.170
this feels kinda weird.

11:01.090 --> 11:04.750
It's kind of embarrassing seeing you like this.

11:05.980 --> 11:08.500
It's the first time I've seen you cry.

11:38.810 --> 11:39.730
Nibi...

11:47.470 --> 11:48.640
Nibi!

12:11.230 --> 12:12.370
Hey...

12:15.180 --> 12:21.470
About how you thought our lives wouldn't have any meaning unless we left the Mud Whale...

12:23.140 --> 12:25.710
I used to agree with you.

12:29.640 --> 12:33.530
But... the truth is...

12:39.230 --> 12:43.830
More than you probably thought... well...

12:48.060 --> 12:50.170
I was content.

12:52.570 --> 12:56.400
Living on that island while yearning for the outside world,

12:58.400 --> 13:02.380
looking at the same sky and sea as you every day...

13:05.390 --> 13:06.730
Even just that...

13:10.140 --> 13:11.180
was the best!

13:20.600 --> 13:21.900
That's not it.

13:23.310 --> 13:26.840
It was me... who lacked meaning.

13:31.760 --> 13:33.700
If I hadn't met them...

13:36.960 --> 13:38.840
If I hadn't been with you...

13:43.920 --> 13:47.510
I would never have found a reason to live!

13:53.870 --> 13:58.480
Ouni... I'll always be waiting for you.

14:05.220 --> 14:06.450
Show it to me.

14:07.590 --> 14:11.660
Cut through the sandstorm and show me the world beyond!

14:37.830 --> 14:40.230
Nibi... Nibi!

14:47.570 --> 14:48.720
Nibi!

15:16.390 --> 15:18.390
Ouni!

15:21.810 --> 15:22.770
Hey.

15:23.160 --> 15:25.060
I'm Olivines.

15:25.840 --> 15:28.530
Oli...vines?

15:29.190 --> 15:32.560
Archivist of Falaina, let's make a deal.

15:32.560 --> 15:33.770
Huh?

15:33.770 --> 15:40.640
Offer all the emotions of the people on
your island to the great nous Anthropos.

15:40.640 --> 15:43.080
If you can promise me that,

15:43.080 --> 15:46.730
I'll give you this, one of Anthropos' kokalo.

15:47.770 --> 15:49.890
Ema lives on Falaina.

15:49.890 --> 15:55.100
If the kokalo and Ema are brought together,
Falaina will be able to advance to a new stage.

15:56.780 --> 15:58.660
I don't really understand.

15:59.420 --> 16:02.060
I have to get back to the Mud Whale
with Lykos and Ouni.

16:06.940 --> 16:08.480
What is this?

16:17.530 --> 16:19.790
Chakuro, does it hurt?

16:23.220 --> 16:28.710
The reason we feel pain is because our heads are saying it hurts.

16:32.650 --> 16:38.290
Everyone is led astray by that pain, damaged, and compelled to make mistakes.

16:47.770 --> 16:49.570
But what if...

16:50.020 --> 16:53.070
we could <i>slightly</i> change things and make it go away?

16:53.680 --> 16:55.050
It's very simple.

16:55.900 --> 16:58.500
Just an alteration of the heart's records.

17:01.080 --> 17:05.080
From all the emotions that the nous has sucked out from different people,

17:05.080 --> 17:11.890
we share only the pleasant fragments and
make them seem like they truly belong to you.

17:18.210 --> 17:20.020
Hey, over here!

17:39.340 --> 17:40.370
How about it?

17:42.180 --> 17:47.210
Doesn't it feel as if this emotion was born of your own heart?

17:53.880 --> 17:55.260
Lykos!

17:55.910 --> 17:57.010
How about it?

18:00.430 --> 18:05.840
You can submerge yourself in this utterly fulfilling world forever.

18:08.250 --> 18:09.350
I know.

18:09.690 --> 18:14.330
It must've hurt so much up to now,
children of the whale.

18:22.060 --> 18:27.780
Let's rewrite your sorrowful story with the power of the nous.

18:28.540 --> 18:32.030
Rewrite... the painful records?

18:32.710 --> 18:37.920
Sinners of Falaina, I want to grant you salvation.

18:43.010 --> 18:44.000
Then...

18:46.340 --> 18:49.710
Then what about our memories of everyone?

18:49.710 --> 18:50.650
Where will they go?

18:52.270 --> 18:57.150
Sami, Lady Taisha, Nibi, and everyone else are gone.

18:58.310 --> 18:58.990
Even so,

19:00.410 --> 19:02.920
they were all here with us.

19:02.920 --> 19:06.630
That itself is the proof that they lived.

19:06.630 --> 19:08.570
I can't forget them.

19:09.280 --> 19:11.380
The pain and suffering and everything else...

19:13.050 --> 19:15.840
are the records of our lives.

19:34.170 --> 19:36.980
Why are you giving me this?

19:38.020 --> 19:39.780
I can't keep our promise.

19:40.310 --> 19:41.600
It's fine.

19:42.220 --> 19:45.450
I want to see where your choice leads.

19:47.990 --> 19:54.080
Carry on, sinners of Falaina, to a new world!

20:31.600 --> 20:32.870
Let's go, Lykos!

20:39.420 --> 20:43.910
<i>93 Sand Era. Seventeenth day of the seventh month.</i>

20:45.000 --> 20:49.460
<i>The sandstorm that began that morning started to wane in the evening.</i>

20:51.520 --> 21:01.570
<i>As we were planning our escape from Skylos, the winds,
as if to contrast the collapsing ship, were calm.</i>

21:10.890 --> 21:16.210
<i>It was very painful to have to leave our fallen comrades behind.</i>

21:17.470 --> 21:24.620
<i>However, engraving their memories into
our hearts, we vowed never to forget them,</i>

21:25.270 --> 21:27.550
<i>and departed at last.</i>

21:34.340 --> 21:42.820
<i>Unaccustomed to fighting as we were, we willfully took up arms and rebelled against our fates.</i>

21:45.480 --> 21:52.050
<i>Fighting was the only recourse available to protect our paradise.</i>

22:26.280 --> 22:31.100
<i>Many of our friends died and returned to the Sand Ocean.</i>

22:31.840 --> 22:39.880
<i>I wished only to write everything down as proof of their lives.</i>

22:44.480 --> 22:52.350
<i>As a survivor, and as the archivist, that was my reason for living.</i>
